From d9b9232cc5bc899d2cf9b7e4ed073da941b26027 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:15:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] rc, shared: file modes, secrets at rest, private daemon
 configs (2026-11-03 review) (102.8 line)

- f_write() creates 0644 when the caller names no mode (was 0666); /tmp/reboot and /tmp/upgrade
  count only when root made them (f_root_owned / f_read_root_string: watchdog, sched_daemon,
  check_watchdog).
- Boot: /data 0700 and the kernel nvram file 0600 right after the mount; /var/lock, /var/tmp/dhcp
  and /tmp/mnt 0755, rc lock files 0600; the Broadcom device nodes, kmsg, kmem and raw disk nodes
  0600 (new disks too, through asus_sd / asus_sg); /proc/driver loses group/other write;
  kptr_restrict=2, dmesg_restrict=1, panic_on_oops=1; /jffs/cert.tgz 0600; /var/state/parport
  sticky; /etc/email 0755.
- avahi, the notification centre and netool keep their directories through reaper_secure_dir();
  mount_r() refuses a mount point that is not a directory.
- 0600: the PPP / PPTP / L2TP option files, the WireGuard PSK file, authorized_keys. 0644: the SDN
  and VPN resolver lists. Captive-portal hooks 0700, portal web roots 0755.
- chpass(): login:password goes to chpasswd on a pipe (no temp file, no argv); a colon in the
  login or a line break in either is refused.
- The hostapd / wpa_supplicant configs (every start path, the WPS restarts included) and the
  AiMesh daemon start under umask 077. /etc/pam.d is root 0755 (it holds the OpenVPN server's PAM
  policy).
- restore_cert(): restored certificates 0644, keys 0600 (tar kept an older archive's modes).
- libdisk add_folder() restores the umask it cleared; at every mount the volume-root
  share-permission files lose group/other write.
- Gatekeeper: the sinkhole logs to its own file (it used to take /dev/null); on an HTTPS-only GUI
  start_gk() starts the plain-HTTP instance that serves the waiting page.
- rexport refuses control characters in its settings. The LLTD responder and client are not
  started. The hotspot config no longer names ip-up / ip-down scripts nothing generates.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
